  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 6",
  "description": "Release 6 of the HBN-EEG dataset, the EEG component of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network project, organized in BIDS format. It contains EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 134 participants aged 5-21 performing three passive tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching) and three active tasks (contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Events carry HED annotations, and psychopathology factors derived from the CBCL (p-factor, attention, internalizing, externalizing) are provided alongside basic quality-control results.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded while children and adolescents completed six tasks: resting state with eyes open/closed, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, and symbol search. Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files with HED annotations. Minimal quality control checked file integrity and the presence of required events.",
